  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The formula \\(N=8\\cdot10^8\\cdot x^{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\) gives, for a certain group, the number of individuals whose income exceeds \\(x\\) dollars. The lowest income, in dollars, of the wealthiest \\(800\\) individuals is at least:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(10^4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(10^6\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(10^8\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(10^{12}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(10^{16}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "10000"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1960-p17.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "At the cutoff, \\[ 800=8\\cdot10^8x^{-\\frac{3}{2}}. \\] Hence \\(x^{\\frac{3}{2}}=10^6,\\) and raising both sides to the \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\) power gives \\(x=10^4.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Set \\(N=800\\) at the income cutoff",
        "After simplifying powers of \\(10,\\) solve \\(x^{\\frac{3}{2}}=10^6\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
